      "short": "substituted; 20; 10, 0.2.",
      "worked": "They substituted $q:r=10:3$ into $p:q:r$. Since $p$ is $20\\%$ of $q$, $p=0.2q$. Using representative ratio parts $q=10$ and $r=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}p&=0.2q\\\\p&=0.2(10)\\\\p&=2\\end{align*}$$\nHence $p:q:r=2:10:3$.",
